CONVENȚIE EHS CONTRACTORI/ CONTRACTOR HSE AGREEMENT
Document anexat la Contractul nr. 4501270935/09.06.2026
The document annexed to the Contract no. 4501270935/09.06.2026

Limba Română English Language
CONVENTIE PRIVIND SECURITATEA SI SANATATEA IN MUNCA, SITUATIILE DE URGENTA SI PROTECTIA MEDIULUI
Prezenta Conventie se incheie in conformitate cu legislatia si actele normative in vigoare (Legea nr. 319/2006 a securitatii si sanatatii in munca, H.G. 1425/2006 cu modificarile si completarile ulterioare pentru aprobarea Normelor metodologice de aplicare a Legii 319/2006, Legea 307/2006 privind apararea impotriva incendiilor, Ordin nr. 163/2007 privind aprobarea Normelor generale de aparare impotriva incendiilor, Ordonanță de urgență 195/2005 privind protecţia mediului, Regulamentul 1907/2006 privind înregistrarea, evaluarea, autorizarea şi restricţionarea substanţelor chimice (REACH)). AGREEMENT REGARDING OCCUPATIONAL HEALTH AND SAFETY, EMERGENCY SITUATIONS AND ENVIRONMENTAL PROTECTION
This agreement is concluded in accordance with the applicable Romanian legislation and regulations in force (Law no. 319/2006 on Occupational Health and Safety, Government Decision 1425/2006 approving the methodological norms for the application of Law 319/2006, Law 307/2006 on fire protection, Order 163/2007 approving the General Fire Protection Rules, Emergency Ordinance 195/2005 regarding environmental protection and Regulation (EC) 1907/2006 concerning the Registration, Evaluation, Authorisation and Restriction of Chemicals – REACH).

I. Obiectul conventiei
Prin prezenta conventie se stabilesc obligatiile si responsabilitatile partilor privind organizarea activitatii de prevenire si protectie, cercetarea si inregistrarea evenimentelor pe linia Securitatii si Sanatatii Muncii, privind Situatiile de Urgenta si Protectia Mediului in vederea evitarii producerii de incidente tehnice/ accidente de munca/ incendii/ poluarii accidentale.

I. Subject of the Agreement
This agreement establishes the obligations and responsibilities of the parties regarding the organisation of prevention and protection activities, the investigation and recording of Occupational Health and Safety events, as well as Emergency and Environmental protection measures in order to prevent technical incidents, work accidents, fires or accidental pollution.

II. 1. Obligatii si Responsabilitati – Obligatii comune
fiecare parte contractanta este obligata sa asigure respectarea reglementarilor legale privind Securitatea si Sanatatea in Munca, Situatiile de Urgenta si Protectia Mediului, specifice activitatii desfasurate de personalul propriu, fara sa se poata transfera, in nici un fel, aceste responsabilitati catre cealalta Parte contractanta;
sa desfasoare activitatile in asa fel incat sa nu expuna la pericol de accidentare sau imbolnavire profesionala atat personalului propriu, cat si celelalte persoane participante la procesul de munca;
partile contractante pot controla, prin personal de specialitate, modul de respectare a prevederilor de Securitatea si Sanatatea in Munca, Situatiile de Urgenta si Protectia Mediului in vigoare;
continuarea activitatii in conditii de securitate necorespunzatoare sau cu vicii ascunse (tehnice sau organizatorice) este interzisa, oricare consecinte ale continuarii activitatii in astfel de conditii fiind suportate de partea in culpa;
in cazul aparitiei unor noi factori de risc sau pericole, partile contractante se vor informa reciproc si operativ pentru stabilirea noilor masuri de securitate ce se impun pentru prevenirea unor incidente/ accidente de munca;
in conditiile producerii unor avarii, incendii sau explozii, partile au obligatia de a colabora si participa cu formatii proprii sau mijloace tehnice din dotare pentru inlaturarea acestor evenimente si pentru salvarea persoanelor si a bunurilor materiale;
se interzice consumul de bauturi alcoolice, substante halucinogene sau prezentarea la serviciu a angajatilor proprii in stare fizica necorespunzatoare, echipati cu echipament individual de protectie necorespunzator sau incomplet;
se interzice patrunderea angajatilor proprii in zonele de lucru cu mijloace de aprindere, introducerea si folosirea surselor de foc la locurile de munca unde pot aparea atmosfere potential explozive;
se interzice fumatul pe teritoriul Beneficiarului, acesta fiind permis doar in locurile special amenajate si semnalizate.
II. 2. Obligatii BENEFICIAR
sa instruiasca lucratorii Executantului privind activitatile specifice Beneficiarului, riscurile privind Securitatea si Sanatatea in Munca, riscurile de incendiu, poluare accidentala, precum si masurile si activitatile de prevenire si protectie la nivelul societatii, in general, consemnadu-se in fisa de instruire colectiva, conform Anexei nr. 12 din HG nr 1425/2006 actualizata, intocmita in doua exemplare, din care un exemplar va ramane la Beneficiar, iar celalalt exemplar se va transmite Executantului; Instruirea se va face de catre reprezentantul Beneficiarului in limba romana, la instruire fiind obligatorie prezenta unui translator (traducator) care sa traduca tematica in limba vorbita, inteleasa de catre lucratorii Executantului;
sa aduca la cunostinta Executantului regulile de circulatie in incinta societatii, caile de acces, de interventie si de evacuare;
sa puna la dispozitia Executantului dotarile si utilitatile necesare, spatiile de lucru si echipamentele de munca prevazute in contract;
sa puna la dispozitia Executantului instructiunile proprii SSM privind utilizarea echipamentelor de munca ale Beneficiarului, la care lucratorii isi desfasoara activitatea, lucrarea de evaluare de riscuri si Planul de Prevenire si Protectie in format PDF, in limba romana, precum si fisele cu date de securitate ale substantelor chimice utilizate de lucratorii Executantului;
Beneficiarul isi rezerva dreptul de a nu accepta la lucru angajati ai Executantului care nu sunt instruiti corespunzator conform tuturor fazelor de instruire in domeniul securitatii si sanatatii in munca, a situatiilor de urgenta si protectiei mediului;
lui la înălțime: cască de protecție cu închidere sub bărbie, ham de prindere etc.);
Beneficiarul isi rezerva dreptul de a nu accepta la lucru angajati ai Executantului care nu sunt verificati medical prin cabinet de medicina muncii, precum si pe cei care nu respecta recomandarile medicale;
Beneficiarul isi rezerva dreptul de a suspenda lucrarile Executantului, in cazul observarii unor abateri de la standardele de mediu, Securitați si Sanatatii in Munca si Situatiilor de Urgenta, pana la intrarea in conformitate cu acestea si va indica in scris care sunt abaterile, modalitatea de remediere a acestora si termenele de restabilire a situatiei anterioare.
II. 3. Obligatii EXECUTANT si reprezentantii acestuia (subcontractori):
reprezentantii Executantului se vor prezenta in prima zi de lucru la sediul Beneficiarului, in vederea informarii asupra riscurilor existente pe perimetrul societatii si completarea fisei colective de instruire, conform Anexei nr.12 din HG nr 1425/2006 actualizata; intrucat instruirea se face de catre reprezentantul Beneficiarului in limba romana, la instruire este obligatorie prezenta unui translator (traducator) care sa traduca tematica in limba vorbita de catre lucratorii Executantului; Executantul va comunica in scris Beneficiarului, la inceperea lucrarilor, numele persoanei desemnate ca si sef direct al lucratorilor Executantului, care va avea atributii de coordonare a echipei de lucru, de supraveghere a desfasurarii activitatilor in conformitate cu instructiunile prelucrate si legislatia SSM, SU si PM.; Executantul are obligatia de a informa Beneficiarul in scris, despre noii angajati, pentru instruirea privind activitățile specifice din Stabilus, riscurile SSM și măsurile de prevenire și protecție, în general;
lucratorii Executantului sunt obligati sa respecte prevederile legislatiei in domeniul Securitatii si Sanatatii in Munca, a Situatiilor de Urgenta si Protectiei Mediului pe teritoriul Beneficiarului;
Executantul se obligă să respecte prevederile legale aplicabile în domeniul sănătății și securității în muncă și să întreprindă toate formalitățile necesare pentru organizarea activităţilor de prevenire şi protecţie prin intermediul personalului propriu (responsabil SSM propriu) sau prin intermediul serviciilor externe, în vederea desfaşurării sesiunilor de instruire, necesare în functie de activităţile efectuate. Executantul se obligă să comunice Beneficiarului, imediat după constatare, orice încălcare a normelor de siguranţă şi securitate, sau a oricărei situaţii de pericol iminent;
Executantul este exclusiv responsabil pentru respectarea tuturor prevederilor aplicabile în vederea asigurării securităţii şi sănătăţii în muncă de către personalul propriu, în toate aspectele legate de executarea obligaţiilor privind serviciile prestate în baza Contractului.
Executantul se obliga sa asigure efectuarea lucrarilor din contract, cu personal instruit/calificat/autorizat, conform legislatiei in vigoare, in functie de specificul lucrarilor executate, a conditiilor si mediului de lucru;
Executantul, prin personal propriu, isi va instrui, prin metode proprii, angajatii sai cu prevederile de Securitate si Sanatate in Munca, Situatii de Urgenta si Protectia Mediului (riscurile specifice si masurile de prevenire a producerii accidentelor, cu instructiuni proprii SSM privind operatiile, activitatile executate, echipamentele de lucru pe care le folosesc, precum si cu masurile de prevenire a incendiilor, poluarilor sau altor incidente periculoase specifice lucrarilor executate etc.);
Executantul, prin personal propriu, va verifica insusirea prevederilor Securitatii si Sanatatii in Munca, a Situatiilor de Urgenta si Protectiei Mediului, a personalului propriu instruit si se va asigura ca acestia au inteles in clar informatiile transmise, pe care le vor aplica corespunzator pe teritoriul Beneficiarului;
reprezentantii Executantul trebuie sa utilizeze spatiul si echipamentele de munca puse la dispozitie de Beneficiar, conform clauzelor contractuale; in cazul executarii unor lucrari care necesita diferite organizari speciale, perimetrari la locul de munca, protejarea ariei de lucru etc, Executantul se obliga sa isi semnalizeze zona respectiva conform legislatiei SSM cu mijloace proprii (banda, panouri etc.) si sa ia toate masurile necesare pentru interzicerea accesului persoanelor neautorizate etc.;
Executantul va utiliza doar substantele/ amestecurile chimice agreate a fi folosite pe teritoriul Beneficiarului, conform fiselor cu date de securitate, aflate la locul de munca;
reprezentantii Executantului nu vor bloca caile de acces, interventie si evacuare cu materiale si vor intretine curatenia in zona de lucru. In cazul in care prin natura lucrarilor efectuate este necesara blocarea partiala sau totala a cailor de evacuare, va informa Beneficiarul, pentru ca acesta sa-si ia masurile necesare in timp util.;
in cazul producerii unor avarii/ incendii/ explozii reprezentantii Executantului vor participa impreuna cu angajatii Beneficiarului pentru inlaturarea acestor evenimente, pentru salvarea persoanelor si a bunurilor materiale;
reprezentantii Executantului au obligatia sa nu intervina la instalatii electrice, instalatii de semnalizare, sistemele de protectie ale echipamentelor de munca din dotarea Beneficiarului, să utilizeze corect maşinile, utilajele, echipamentele, instalaţiile puse la dispozitie de Beneficiar conform Cartilor Tehnice emise de producator si a Instructiunilor de lucru intocmite de catre Stabilus pentru echipamentele de munca, tehnologia de lucru si sa nu intre in spatii semnalizate cu accesul interzis. Executantul are obligatia de a nu influenta sub nici o forma procesele de munca, cladirile, utilajelele si instalatiile sau activitatea Beneficiarului;
sa asigure dotarea personalului propriu cu echipament individual de protectie certificat, specific riscurilor activitatii desfasurate in Stabilus (salopeta si manusi de protectie rezistente la uzura, incaltaminte de protectie tip S3+ESD, imbracaminte pentru sezonul rece). Echipamentul individual de protective specific altor operatii in afara contractului, se va suporta de catre Beneficiar. De asemenea, Executantul se obliga sa instruiasca personalul propriu cu privire la obligatia purtarii EIP-ului din dotare si sa nu accepte la lucru persoane echipate incomplet sau necorespunzator;
Executantul va asigura efectuarea controlului medical la angajare si pe cel periodic a personalului propriu, in conformitate cu H.G. 355/2007 privind supravegherea sanatatii lucratorilor si completarea fisei de identificarea a factorilor de risc. Executantul se va asigura ca personalul ce efectueaza lucrari specifice (exemplu: la inaltime, electrice) este apt pentru activitatea desfasurata;
Executantul se va asigura ca angajatii proprii desemnati sa desfasoare activitatile cunosc si inteleg procedurile/instructiunile referitoare la cerintele specifice de protectia mediului (referitor la produsele chimice, deseuri). In situatia producerii unui incident/accident din vina sa, Executantul va suporta costul pentru repararea prejudiciului, inlaturarea urmarilor produse de acesta si revenirea la conditiile anterioare producerii prejudiciului.
III. Comunicarea, cercetarea si inregistrarea evenimentelor de munca
In cazul producerii unui eveniment de munca, ambele parti trebuie sa ia urmatoarele masuri:
sa acorde primul ajutor victimelor;
lor care efectuează cercetarea si vor constitui probe în cercetarea evenimentului;
sa ia masuri pentru conservarea probelor privind starea de fapt a producerii evenimentului, in vederea stabilirii cu certitudine a cauzelor si responsabililor de producerea acestuia;
sa avizeze organele de cercetare legale, cand accidentul are ca urmare invaliditate evidenta sau deces.
sa se informeze in scris reciproc, precum si Inspectoratul Teritorial de Munca despre evenimentul produs cu toate datele necesare conform prevederilor legale.
in cazul producerii unui eveniment in care sunt implicati lucratorii Executantului, acesta va informa Beneficiarul in scris despre eveniment, comunicarea acestuia catre organele abilitate se face de catre angajatorul victimei (Executant), iar cercetarea se va face de catre Executant. In cazul in care accidentarea lucratorului Executantului a implicat utilizarea unui echipament de munca, alte dotari tehnice puse la dispozitie de catre Beneficiar sau s-a produs din cauza unui angajat al Beneficiarului, din comisia de cercetare va face parte si un membru din cadrul Beneficiarului;
inregistrarea accidentelor suferite de personalul propriu al Executantului pe teritoriul Beneficiarului, se va efectua de catre Executant, Beneficiarul nu isi asuma legal responsabilitatea accidentelor de munca in care sunt implicati angajatii si/sau subcontractantii sau alti colaboratori ai Executantului.
IV. Dispozitii finale
prezenta conventie se poate modifica numai cu acordul celor doua parti, modificarea unilaterala fiind interzisa;
prevederile stabilite in prezenta conventie sunt valabile pe toata perioada derularii Contractului incheiat intre cele doua parti.
V. Semnaturi II. Obligations and Responsibilities – Common obligations
a. each contracting party is obliged to ensure compliance with the legal regulations regarding Occupational Health and Safety, Emergency Situations, and Environmental Protection, specific to the activities carried out by its own personnel, without being able, in any way, to transfer these responsibilities to the other contracting party;
b. to carry out activities in such a way as not to expose either their own personnel or other persons involved in the work process to the risk of injury or occupational illness;
c. the contracting parties may, through specialized personnel, monitor compliance with the applicable Occupational Health and Safety, Emergency Situations, and Environmental Protection regulations;
d. the continuation of activities under inadequate safety conditions or in the presence of hidden defects (technical or organizational) is prohibited, and any consequences arising from continuing activities under such conditions shall be borne by the party at fault;
e. in the event of new risk factors or hazards arising, the contracting parties shall promptly inform each other in order to establish the necessary safety measures to prevent incidents or work accidents;
f. in the event of damages, fires, or explosions, the parties are obliged to cooperate and participate with their own teams or technical means to eliminate such events and to ensure the rescue of persons and material assets;
g. the consumption of alcoholic beverages or hallucinogenic substances is prohibited, as well as the presence at work of employees in an unfit physical condition or equipped with inadequate or incomplete personal protective equipment;
h. the entry of employees into work areas with ignition sources, as well as the introduction and use of open flames in workplaces where potentially explosive atmospheres may occur, is prohibited;
i. smoking is prohibited on the Beneficiary’s premises and is only permitted in specially designated and marked areas.
II. 2. Beneficiary’ Obligations
a. to instruct the Contractor’s employees regarding the Beneficiary’s specific activities, the Occupational Health and Safety risks, fire risks, accidental pollution risks, as well as the prevention and protection measures and activities at company level in general, such instruction being recorded in the collective training record, in accordance with Annex No. 12 of Government Decision No. 1425/2006, as amended, prepared in two copies, one copy remaining with the Beneficiary and the other being provided to the Contractor; The instruction shall be carried out by the Beneficiary’s representative in Romanian, and the presence of a translator/interpreter is mandatory in order to translate the training content into the language spoken and understood by the Contractor’s employees;
b. to inform the Contractor of the traffic rules within the company premises, as well as the access, intervention, and evacuation routes;
c. to provide the Contractor with the necessary facilities and utilities, workspaces, and work equipment as stipulated in the contract;
d. to provide the Contractor with the Beneficiary’s internal OHS instructions regarding the use of the Beneficiary’s work equipment used by the employees, the risk assessment documentation and the Prevention and Protection Plan in PDF format, in Romanian, as well as the safety data sheets for the chemical substances used by the Contractor’s employees;
e. the Beneficiary reserves the right to deny access to work to the Contractor’s employees who have not been properly trained in all required stages of training in the fields of Occupational Health and Safety, Emergency Situations, and Environmental Protection;
f. the Beneficiary reserves the right to deny access to work to the Contractor’s employees who are not properly equipped with certified personal protective equipment appropriate to the risks of the performed activity and approved by the Beneficiary (protective coveralls and wear-resistant gloves, protective footwear with toe caps, cold-weather clothing, including PPE specific to working at height: protective helmet with chin strap, safety harness etc.);
g. the Beneficiary reserves the right to deny access to work to the Contractor’s employees who have not undergone occupational medical examination, as well as those who do not comply with the medical recommendations;
h. the Beneficiary reserves the right to suspend the Contractor’s works in the event of observed deviations from environmental, Occupational Health and Safety, and Emergency Situations standards, until compliance is achieved, and shall indicate in writing the identified deviations, the corrective measures required, and the deadlines for restoring the previous situation.
II. 3 Obligations THE CONTRACTOR and its representatives (subcontractors):
a. the Contractor’s representatives shall report on the first working day to the Beneficiary’s premises in order to be informed about the risks existing within the company’s perimeter and to complete the collective training record, in accordance with Annex No. 12 of Government Decision No. 1425/2006, as amended; as the training is conducted by the Beneficiary’s representative in Romanian, the presence of a translator/interpreter is mandatory to translate the content into the language spoken by the Contractor’s employees; the Contractor shall notify the Beneficiary in writing, at the commencement of the works, of the name of the person designated as the direct supervisor of the Contractor’s employees, who shall be responsible for coordinating the work team and supervising the performance of activities in accordance with the provided instructions and the applicable OHS, Emergency Situations, and Environmental Protection legislation; the Contractor shall also inform the Beneficiary in writing of any new employees, in order to provide training regarding Stabilus-specific activities, OHS risks, and general prevention and protection measures;
b. the Contractor’s employees are obliged to comply with the provisions of the legislation in the fields of Occupational Health and Safety, Emergency Situations, and Environmental Protection while on the Beneficiary’s premises;
c. the Contractor undertakes to comply with the applicable legal provisions in the field of occupational health and safety and to carry out all necessary formalities for organizing prevention and protection activities through its own personnel (internal OHS responsible person) or through external services, in order to conduct the necessary training sessions depending on the activities performed; the Contractor undertakes to immediately notify the Beneficiary, upon becoming aware, of any breach of safety regulations or any situation of imminent danger;
d. the Contractor is solely responsible for compliance by its own personnel with all applicable provisions regarding occupational health and safety, in all aspects related to the performance of obligations concerning the services provided under the Contract;
e. the Contractor undertakes to perform the works under the contract using trained/qualified/authorized personnel, in accordance with the applicable legislation, depending on the specific nature of the works, working conditions, and work environment;
f. the Contractor, through its own personnel, shall train its employees, using its own methods, on Occupational Health and Safety, Emergency Situations, and Environmental Protection provisions (specific risks and measures for preventing accidents, internal OHS instructions regarding operations and activities performed, work equipment used, as well as measures for preventing fires, pollution, or other hazardous incidents specific to the performed works, etc.);
g. the Contractor, through its own personnel, shall verify the understanding of Occupational Health and Safety, Emergency Situations, and Environmental Protection provisions by its trained personnel and shall ensure that they clearly understand the information provided and apply it properly on the Beneficiary’s premises;
h. the Contractor’s representatives shall use the workspaces and work equipment provided by the Beneficiary in accordance with the contractual clauses; where the execution of works requires special arrangements, worksite demarcation, protection of the work area, etc., the Contractor undertakes to mark the respective area in accordance with OHS legislation using its own means (tape, panels, etc.) and to take all necessary measures to prevent access by unauthorized persons;
i. the Contractor shall use only the chemical substances/mixtures approved for use on the Beneficiary’s premises, in accordance with the safety data sheets available at the workplace;
j. the Contractor’s representatives shall not block access, intervention, or evacuation routes with materials and shall maintain cleanliness in the work area; where, due to the nature of the works, partial or total blocking of evacuation routes is necessary, the Contractor shall inform the Beneficiary so that it can take the necessary measures in due time;
k. in the event of damages, fires, or explosions, the Contractor’s representatives shall cooperate with the Beneficiary’s employees to eliminate such events and to ensure the rescue of persons and material assets;
l. the Contractor’s representatives shall not interfere with electrical installations, signaling installations, or safety systems of the work equipment belonging to the Beneficiary; they shall use correctly the machines, equipment, installations provided by the Beneficiary in accordance with the Technical Manuals issued by the manufacturer and the Work Instructions prepared by Stabilus for the work equipment and technology, and shall not enter areas marked as restricted access; the Contractor is obliged not to influence in any way the work processes, buildings, machinery, installations, or the activity of the Beneficiary;
m. the Contractor shall ensure that its personnel are provided with certified personal protective equipment appropriate to the risks of the activities carried out at Stabilus (protective coveralls and wear-resistant gloves, S3+ESD protective footwear, cold-weather clothing); personal protective equipment specific to operations outside the scope of the contract shall be borne by the Beneficiary; the Contractor also undertakes to instruct its personnel on the obligation to wear the provided PPE and not to allow access to work for persons improperly or incompletely equipped;
n. the Contractor shall ensure that its personnel undergo pre-employment and periodic medical examinations, in accordance with Government Decision No. 355/2007 on the health surveillance of workers, and the completion of the risk factor identification sheet; the Contractor shall ensure that personnel performing specific works (e.g., working at height, electrical works) are medically fit for the activities performed;
o. the Contractor shall ensure that its designated employees performing activities are aware of and understand the procedures/instructions regarding specific environmental protection requirements (relating to chemical products and waste); in the event of an incident/accident caused by its fault, the Contractor shall bear the costs for remedying the damage, eliminating its consequences, and restoring the conditions existing prior to the occurrence of the damage.
III. Communication, Investigation and Recording of Work-Related Events
a) In the event of a work-related incident, both parties shall take the following measures:
provide first aid to the victims;
~
