ሀpreserve the factual situation that led to the occurrence of the event, except in cases where this would lead to the aggravation of the personnel’s condition or the occurrence of similar events; for any modification of the factual situation resulting from the event, the Contractor shall record, under its own responsibility, in a written report, all changes made after the occurrence of the event; the Contractor shall take measures to ensure that sketches and photographs of the place where the event occurred are made, and any objects containing or bearing traces of the event shall be identified and collected. These objects shall be handed over to the authorities conducting the investigation and shall constitute evidence in the investigation of the event;
take measures to preserve evidence regarding the factual circumstances of the event, in order to establish with certainty its causes and those responsible;
notify the competent investigation authorities when the accident results in obvious invalidity or death;
mutually inform each other in writing, as well as the Territorial Labour Inspectorate, about the occurred event, providing all necessary data in accordance with legal provisions.
b) in the event of an occurrence involving the Contractor’s employees, the Contractor shall inform the Beneficiary in writing about the event; notification to the competent authorities shall be made by the employer of the victim (the Contractor), and the investigation shall be carried out by the Contractor. If the injury of the Contractor’s employee involved the use of work equipment or other technical equipment provided by the Beneficiary, or occurred due to an employee of the Beneficiary, a representative of the Beneficiary shall also be part of the investigation committee;
c) the recording of accidents suffered by the Contractor’s own personnel on the Beneficiary’s premises shall be carried out by the Contractor. The Beneficiary does not assume legal responsibility for work accidents involving employees and/or subcontractors or other collaborators of the Contractor.
IV. Final Provisions
a) this agreement may be amended only with the consent of both parties; unilateral modification is prohibited;
b) the provisions set out in this agreement shall remain valid throughout the entire duration of the Contract concluded between the two parties.
V. Signatures

